<title>AUSTRALIA: QNI shares dive on revolt over Gencor deal.</title>
<headline>QNI shares dive on revolt over Gencor deal.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in nickel producer QNI Ltd dived 15 cents or over 5.5 percent to A$2.50 in active early Friday trade as a shareholder revolt against QNI's merger deal with Gencor Ltd gathered momentum.</p>
<p>Institutional investors in particular believed the nickel assets contributed by Gencor to the merged group were over-valued and Gencor had received favourable terms under the deal, brokers said.</p>
<p>The deal had sparked so much opposition it may even fail to pass at a shareholders meeting scheduled to approve the deal, they said.</p>
</text>
